# Movement against the war (War window)
antiwar-line = Movement against the war: { $movement } of its recruits (weariness { $weariness }) · mobilized { $mobilized } of the people · strike { $strike } of the war industry · mutiny { $mutiny } of the land fire
antiwar-tip = The movement recruits among the war-weary. The mobilized march, the workers who back it stop the war industry and the soldiers who back it lose fire. With many mobilized, the government falls below the peace threshold already.
antiwar-memory = When the war began { $memory } of the movement was left; the war support started lower.
antiwar-falls-below-peace = With so many mobilized, the government's fall counts down below { $peace }, not only below the collapse.
antiwar-countdown = Below peace, with the movement in the streets: the government falls in { $count ->
    [one] { $weeks } week
   *[other] { $weeks } weeks
}; until then, peace may still be made on its own terms.
